course: dictionary
lesson: 10730
title: Upholster and upholstered
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe the things in our homes. «The workers will upholster the old sofa in soft blue velvet.» Upholster is a verb, an action word. The clues are sofa, velvet and soft, so it means to cover a sofa or chair with padding and cloth so it is comfy to sit on.
explain: Now look at the ending. «The armchair was upholstered in brown leather.» Here upholstered describes the armchair, so it is an adjective: it tells you what the chair is like. Try swapping in covered with padding: it still makes sense, so you are on the right track.
explain: Upholstery is also a job. «Dad is an upholsterer, and he can re-upholster an old armchair.» An upholsterer is the craftsperson who does this work. Re- means again, so re-upholster means to cover something again with new padding and fabric.
fact: Upholster is a verb, and its other forms are upholsters, upholstered and upholstering.
fact: «Upholster» means to cover a chair, sofa or car seat with padding, springs and cloth or leather.
fact: «Upholstered» can describe something covered in soft padding and fabric, like an upholstered armchair.
fact: An upholsterer is a craftsperson who upholsters furniture, and upholstery is the work and the materials.
fact: The prefix re- means again, so «re-upholster» means to upholster something a second time.
exercise: «The workers will upholster the old sofa with new cloth.» What does upholster mean here? | To throw it out | *To cover with padding and cloth so it is soft to sit on | To paint it bright red | To carry it up the stairs
exercise: «The armchair is upholstered in green velvet.» What does upholstered mean? | Very dirty | *Covered with soft padding and fabric | Folded up flat | Made of wood
exercise: Find and copy the word for the person who does upholstery work: «An upholsterer repaired the car seat.» | car | seat | repaired | *upholsterer
test: What does re-upholster mean in «Dad will re-upholster the old chair»? | To remove the chair from the house | To sit on the chair very quickly | *To cover the chair again with new padding and fabric | To paint the legs of the chair
test: Which job does an upholsterer do? | Cooks food in a restaurant | *Covers furniture with padding and cloth | Mends roads with tar | Drives buses to school
exam: In «a velvet-upholstered seat», what does the word upholstered tell you? | The seat is very old and broken | The seat is outside in the rain | *The seat is covered in soft padding and velvet | The seat is made of wood and has no cushion
